cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, its results, or the leak-free split it produces,
  please cite the accompanying article.
title: >-
  Code, statistics, and models for "A comparative study of deep learning
  approaches for automated burn injury segmentation and severity classification"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility materials for a leak-free, externally validated benchmark of
  deep learning for burn severity classification. Includes the source-grouped
  split builder that removes an augmentation-induced data-leakage artifact, the
  masking ablation, the head-to-head comparison of a standalone classifier
  against a two-stage segmentation pipeline, two external validations, and the
  raw JSON behind every reported number.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Altayeb
    given-names: Ryan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0031-9531"
    affiliation: >-
      Faculty of Computer and Information Systems, Islamic University of
      Madinah, Madinah, Saudi Arabia
  - family-names: Alraddadi
    given-names: Abdulrahman
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-2325-5063"
    affiliation: >-
      Faculty of Computer and Information Systems, Islamic University of
      Madinah, Madinah, Saudi Arabia
  - family-names: Alrehaili
    given-names: Mohannad
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2491-185X"
    affiliation: >-
      Faculty of Computer and Information Systems, Islamic University of
      Madinah, Madinah, Saudi Arabia
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/Just-Ryan/burn-severity-benchmark"
keywords:
  - burn severity assessment
  - deep learning
  - data leakage
  - external validation
  - image segmentation
  - reproducibility

